<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Hunnic Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">370 CE – 469 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The nomadic empire whose arrival in Europe set the Goths in motion and which, under Attila, held both halves of the Roman Empire to ransom.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> appeared north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> around 370, defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/greuthungi">Greuthungi</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ermanaric">Ermanaric</a>, which drove the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tervingi">Tervingi</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into Roman territory. Their origins further east are uncertain, though many scholars connect them with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>. By the 420s they had moved their centre to the Hungarian plain.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hun power rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mounted-archer">mounted archers</a> and on a confederation of subject peoples, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/akatziri">Akatziri</a>. Kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rugila">Rua</a>, and then the brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleda">Bleda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>, extracted huge annual payments in gold from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> through treaties such as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-margus">Margus</a> in 435. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/priscus">Priscus</a>, who visited Attila's court in 449, describes wooden palaces, Gothic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> speakers, and an elite enriched by tribute and plunder.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila's</a> defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains">Catalaunian Plains</a> in 451, his raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 452 and his death in 453, the subject peoples revolted under the Gepid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardaric">Ardaric</a> and won at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nedao">Nedao</a> in 454. Attila's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dengizich">Dengizich</a> was killed in 469, and the remaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> merged into later steppe peoples.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hunnic-empire.jpg" alt="Hunnic Empire" width="320" height="310"><figcaption>Image: Slovenski Volk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huns450.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>370 CE – 469 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rua, Bleda, Attila</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hunnic steppe religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hunnic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Huns, Empire of Attila</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=420&amp;focus=hunnic-empire" aria-label="Hunnic Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5137 517 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hunnic Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d=